  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.9\n- Added support for passing a Cancel Token down the stack for the async methods in data core\n- Marking anything that uses DbDataAdapter as obsolete as we are going to remove this is v4.0  it is still supported and included in modern .NET runtimes, but it is considered a legacy technology that receives no new feature updates.\n- Added support for low-overhead async execution:\n- Default / Low-Overhead: Use ExecuteAsync to await database I/O, then read rows synchronously via ToListOf() to eliminate per-row async state machine allocations.\n- Fully Non-Blocking: Use ToListOfAsync() if non-blocking iteration across all rows is required.\n\nv3.7\n- Added build packages for .NET 10\n\nv3.6\n- Add support filling an object that has the new required word\n\nv.3.5\n- Added build packages for .NET 9\n- Added SqlStringBuilder for abstract Bulding on sql statements\n- Add support TimeOnly and DateOnly in the ExecuteScalarWithConvert methods",
